{
  "classes": [
    {
      "id": "obvious",
      "name": "Obvious exposures",
      "applies": {
        "always": true
      },
      "invariant": "No secret, debug switch or dangerous dynamic evaluation is reachable from the repository as shipped.",
      "look": [
        "A hit for a secret pattern: is the value real (not a placeholder, a test fixture or a public key id)? Where is it used, and who can read the repository or the built artifact?",
        "A committed secret file (.env, *.pem, *.key, credentials.json, id_rsa): is it in git history even if deleted now? `git log --all --diff-filter=D --name-only -- <path>`.",
        "A debug or dev switch (DEBUG=True, dev mode, verbose errors): can a request, header or environment variable turn it on in production?",
        "eval/exec/Function/vm with a value that is not a literal: where does the string come from?",
        "A TODO or FIXME about auth, validation or permissions: is the gap it describes still open?",
        "Manifests without a lockfile, or a lockfile that is not used by the install command: what version is installed in CI?"
      ],
      "counts": "A real credential or token readable by anyone with the repository or the artifact, a debug switch reachable from a request, or an eval of outside data.",
      "hardening": "An example value, a placeholder, a public identifier, a missing lockfile with pinned ranges and no exposure.",
      "patterns": [
        {
          "name": "private key block",
          "langs": [
            "any"
          ],
          "needle": "PRIVATE KEY",
          "regex": "-----BEGIN [A-Z ]*PRIVATE KEY-----"
        },
        {
          "name": "AWS access key id",
          "langs": [
            "any"
          ],
          "needle": "AKIA",
          "regex": "\\bAKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}\\b"
        },
        {
          "name": "GitHub token",
          "langs": [
            "any"
          ],
          "needle": "gh",
          "regex": "\\bgh[pousr]_[A-Za-z0-9]{36,}\\b"
        },
        {
          "name": "Slack token",
          "langs": [
            "any"
          ],
          "needle": "xox",
          "regex": "\\bxox[baprs]-[A-Za-z0-9-]{10,}\\b"
        },
        {
          "name": "Stripe live key",
          "langs": [
            "any"
          ],
          "needle": "sk_live_",
          "regex": "\\bsk_live_[A-Za-z0-9]{16,}\\b"
        },
        {
          "name": "Google API key",
          "langs": [
            "any"
          ],
          "needle": "AIza",
          "regex": "\\bAIza[0-9A-Za-z_-]{35}\\b"
        },
        {
          "name": "JWT literal",
          "langs": [
            "any"
          ],
          "needle": "eyJ",
          "regex": "\\beyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{10,}\\.eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{10,}\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{10,}"
        },
        {
          "name": "password or secret assigned a literal",
          "langs": [
            "any"
          ],
          "needle": "=",
          "regex": "(?i)\\b(password|passwd|secret|api[_-]?key|access[_-]?token|auth[_-]?token|client[_-]?secret)\\b\\s*[:=]\\s*[\"'][^\"'\\s]{8,}[\"']"
        },
        {
          "name": "connection string with password",
          "langs": [
            "any"
          ],
          "needle": "://",
          "regex": "(?i)\\b(postgres|postgresql|mysql|mongodb|redis|amqp)://[^:\\s/]+:[^@\\s]{4,}@"
        },
        {
          "name": "debug switched on",
          "langs": [
            "any"
          ],
          "needle": "DEBUG",
          "regex": "\\bDEBUG\\s*[:=]\\s*(True|true|1|\"true\"|'true'|\"1\")"
        },
        {
          "name": "eval or exec of a non-literal",
          "langs": [
            "py"
          ],
          "needle": "e",
          "regex": "\\b(eval|exec)\\s*\\(\\s*[^\"'\\s)]"
        },
        {
          "name": "eval, Function or vm of a non-literal",
          "langs": [
            "js"
          ],
          "needle": "(",
          "regex": "\\b(eval|new\\s+Function|vm\\.runIn\\w+)\\s*\\(\\s*[^\"'\\s)(]"
        },
        {
          "name": "security TODO",
          "langs": [
            "any"
          ],
          "needle": "O",
          "regex": "(?i)\\b(TODO|FIXME|HACK|XXX)\\b.*\\b(auth|authz|authn|permission|validate|validation|sanitize|escape|csrf|security|insecure|secret|password)"
        }
      ],
      "files": [
        {
          "name": "secret file committed",
          "glob": [
            ".env",
            ".env.*",
            "*.pem",
            "*.key",
            "*.p12",
            "*.pfx",
            "*.jks",
            "*.keystore",
            "id_rsa",
            "id_dsa",
            "id_ecdsa",
            "id_ed25519",
            "credentials.json",
            "service-account*.json",
            "*.tfstate",
            ".npmrc",
            ".pypirc",
            ".netrc",
            "*.ovpn"
          ],
          "note": "A credential file in the repository: check its content and its history."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "dependencies",
      "name": "Known vulnerable dependencies",
      "live": "osv",
      "applies": {
        "files": [
          "package-lock.json",
          "yarn.lock",
          "pnpm-lock.yaml",
          "requirements*.txt",
          "poetry.lock",
          "Pipfile.lock",
          "uv.lock",
          "pdm.lock",
          "Cargo.lock",
          "go.mod",
          "Gemfile.lock",
          "composer.lock",
          "packages.lock.json",
          "pom.xml"
        ]
      },
      "invariant": "No dependency the project ships at its pinned version has a known vulnerability that this project's use of it can reach.",
      "look": [
        "For each advisory: which function or feature of the package is affected (the advisory says), and does this project call it? `grep -rn \"<package>\"` for the import, then read graph://used-by/<function> for the call sites.",
        "Does outside data reach that call (a request field, a file, a message)? A vulnerable parser fed only with the project's own constants is not reachable.",
        "Is the fixed version a drop-in (same major) or a breaking upgrade? Name it either way.",
        "A transitive dependency: which direct dependency pulls it in (`npm ls <pkg>`, `pipdeptree`, `cargo tree -i <pkg>`, `go mod why <pkg>`)."
      ],
      "counts": "An advisory whose affected code this project reaches with outside data, at the pinned version.",
      "hardening": "An advisory in a package the project does not call that way: note the upgrade to the fixed version.",
      "patterns": []
    },
    {
      "id": "injection",
      "name": "Injection",
      "applies": {
        "langs": [
          "py",
          "js",
          "go",
          "rs",
          "java",
          "rb",
          "php",
          "c",
          "cs",
          "swift",
          "sh"
        ]
      },
      "invariant": "Data from outside never changes the structure of a command, query, template, path or expression; it is only ever a value.",
      "look": [
        "Shell: a command string built with a variable (shell=True, os.system, exec/execSync with a template string, sh -c, Runtime.exec with a string, system()). The fix is an argument list.",
        "SQL and other queries: a query string built with +, f-string, format, template literal or sprintf and run with execute/query/raw. The fix is a placeholder.",
        "Templates and HTML: a template built from a string, |safe or Markup(), autoescape off, render_template_string, innerHTML, v-html.",
        "Deserialization of outside bytes: pickle, yaml.load without SafeLoader, ObjectInputStream, unserialize, Marshal.load, BinaryFormatter.",
        "Expressions: eval, exec, Function, template engines evaluating user text, regex built from user text (ReDoS, injection), LDAP or XPath strings.",
        "Second-order: data stored safely and used later in another sink (a stored name becomes a file path, a slug becomes a query, a header becomes a log line)."
      ],
      "counts": "A value a lower-trust party controls reaches the sink unparameterized, with a result: another user's data, a file outside the intended folder, a command, a script in another user's page.",
      "hardening": "A sink fed only by literals, configuration the operator writes, or a value validated against an allowlist you read.",
      "patterns": [
        {
          "name": "shell=True",
          "langs": [
            "py"
          ],
          "needle": "shell=True",
          "regex": "shell\\s*=\\s*True"
        },
        {
          "name": "os.system or os.popen",
          "langs": [
            "py"
          ],
          "needle": "os.",
          "regex": "\\bos\\.(system|popen)\\s*\\("
        },
        {
          "name": "query built from a string",
          "langs": [
            "py"
          ],
          "needle": "execute",
          "regex": "\\.(execute|executemany|executescript|raw|extra)\\s*\\(\\s*(f[\"']|[\"'][^\"']*[\"']\\s*(%|\\+)|.*\\.format\\()"
        },
        {
          "name": "query string with %, + or f-string",
          "langs": [
            "py"
          ],
          "needle": "SELECT",
          "regex": "(?i)(f[\"'][^\"']*\\b(select|insert|update|delete)\\b|\\b(select|insert|update|delete)\\b[^\"']*[\"']\\s*(%|\\+)\\s*\\w)"
        },
        {
          "name": "unsafe deserialization",
          "langs": [
            "py"
          ],
          "needle": "load",
          "regex": "\\b(pickle|cPickle|dill|shelve|marshal)\\.loads?\\s*\\(|yaml\\.(load|load_all|unsafe_load)\\s*\\([^)]*\\)(?![^\\n]*SafeLoader)|yaml\\.load\\s*\\([^)]*Loader\\s*=\\s*yaml\\.(Loader|UnsafeLoader|FullLoader)"
        },
        {
          "name": "template from a string or markup",
          "langs": [
            "py"
          ],
          "needle": "a",
          "regex": "\\b(render_template_string|Markup)\\s*\\(|\\|\\s*safe\\b|autoescape\\s*=\\s*False"
        },
        {
          "name": "child_process exec with a template",
          "langs": [
            "js"
          ],
          "needle": "exec",
          "regex": "(?<![.\\w/)\\]])(exec|execSync|spawn|spawnSync)\\s*\\(\\s*(`[^`]*\\$\\{|[^\"'`)\\s][^)]*shell\\s*:\\s*true|[a-zA-Z_$][\\w.$]*\\s*[,)])|child_process\\.(exec|execSync|spawn|spawnSync)\\s*\\(\\s*[^\"'`)\\s]"
        },
        {
          "name": "query built with a template literal",
          "langs": [
            "js"
          ],
          "needle": "`",
          "regex": "\\.(query|execute|raw|unsafe)\\s*\\(\\s*`[^`]*\\$\\{"
        },
        {
          "name": "query built by concatenation",
          "langs": [
            "js"
          ],
          "needle": "+",
          "regex": "(?i)[\"']\\s*(select|insert|update|delete|where)\\b[^\"']*[\"']\\s*\\+\\s*\\w"
        },
        {
          "name": "HTML sink",
          "langs": [
            "js",
            "html"
          ],
          "needle": "HTML",
          "regex": "\\.(innerHTML|outerHTML)\\s*=|insertAdjacentHTML\\s*\\(|dangerouslySetInnerHTML|document\\.write(ln)?\\s*\\("
        },
        {
          "name": "v-html or {@html}",
          "langs": [
            "js",
            "html"
          ],
          "needle": "html",
          "regex": "\\bv-html\\s*=|\\{@html\\b"
        },
        {
          "name": "sh -c with a variable",
          "langs": [
            "go"
          ],
          "needle": "exec.Command",
          "regex": "exec\\.Command(Context)?\\s*\\(\\s*(\"(sh|bash|/bin/sh|/bin/bash|cmd)\"|[a-zA-Z_][\\w.]*\\s*[,)])"
        },
        {
          "name": "query built with Sprintf or +",
          "langs": [
            "go"
          ],
          "needle": "Query",
          "regex": "\\.(Query|QueryRow|Exec|QueryContext|ExecContext|Raw)\\s*\\((ctx,\\s*)?(fmt\\.Sprintf|[\"'][^\"']*[\"']\\s*\\+|\\w+\\s*\\+)"
        },
        {
          "name": "template.HTML or JS cast",
          "langs": [
            "go"
          ],
          "needle": "template.",
          "regex": "template\\.(HTML|JS|URL|HTMLAttr)\\s*\\("
        },
        {
          "name": "sh -c or a shell command string",
          "langs": [
            "rs"
          ],
          "needle": "Command::new",
          "regex": "Command::new\\s*\\(\\s*\"(sh|bash|/bin/sh|cmd)\"|\\.arg\\s*\\(\\s*\"-c\"\\s*\\)"
        },
        {
          "name": "query built with format!",
          "langs": [
            "rs"
          ],
          "needle": "format!",
          "regex": "(query|execute|prepare|sql)\\w*\\s*\\(\\s*&?\\s*format!\\s*\\("
        },
        {
          "name": "Runtime.exec or ProcessBuilder with a string",
          "langs": [
            "java"
          ],
          "needle": "exec",
          "regex": "Runtime\\.getRuntime\\(\\)\\.exec\\s*\\(\\s*[^\"\\s)]|new\\s+ProcessBuilder\\s*\\(\\s*\"(sh|bash|cmd)"
        },
        {
          "name": "query built with + or format",
          "langs": [
            "java"
          ],
          "needle": "Statement",
          "regex": "(?i)(createStatement\\s*\\(|createQuery\\s*\\(\\s*\"[^\"]*\"\\s*\\+|execute(Query|Update)?\\s*\\(\\s*\"[^\"]*\"\\s*\\+|String\\.format\\s*\\(\\s*\"(select|insert|update|delete))"
        },
        {
          "name": "ObjectInputStream or XMLDecoder",
          "langs": [
            "java"
          ],
          "needle": "new ",
          "regex": "new\\s+(ObjectInputStream|XMLDecoder)\\s*\\("
        },
        {
          "name": "shell with interpolation",
          "langs": [
            "rb"
          ],
          "needle": "#{",
          "regex": "(`[^`]*#\\{|\\b(system|exec|spawn|popen)\\s*\\(?\\s*\"[^\"]*#\\{|IO\\.popen\\s*\\(?\\s*\"[^\"]*#\\{)"
        },
        {
          "name": "query with interpolation",
          "langs": [
            "rb"
          ],
          "needle": "#{",
          "regex": "\\.(where|find_by_sql|execute|select_all|order|group|having|joins)\\s*\\(?\\s*\"[^\"]*#\\{"
        },
        {
          "name": "unsafe deserialization",
          "langs": [
            "rb"
          ],
          "needle": "load",
          "regex": "\\b(Marshal\\.load|YAML\\.load(?!_file\\(.*safe)|Oj\\.load)\\s*\\("
        },
        {
          "name": "shell or eval",
          "langs": [
            "php"
          ],
          "needle": "(",
          "regex": "\\b(exec|shell_exec|system|passthru|popen|proc_open|eval)\\s*\\(\\s*\\$"
        },
        {
          "name": "query with a variable",
          "langs": [
            "php"
          ],
          "needle": "$",
          "regex": "(?i)\\b(mysqli?_query|->query|->exec|pg_query)\\s*\\(.*\\$\\w+|\"(select|insert|update|delete)\\b[^\"]*\\$\\w+"
        },
        {
          "name": "unserialize",
          "langs": [
            "php"
          ],
          "needle": "unserialize",
          "regex": "\\bunserialize\\s*\\("
        },
        {
          "name": "system or popen with a built string",
          "langs": [
            "c"
          ],
          "needle": "(",
          "regex": "\\b(system|popen|execl|execlp)\\s*\\(\\s*[a-zA-Z_]\\w*\\s*[,)]"
        },
        {
          "name": "query built with sprintf or +",
          "langs": [
            "c"
          ],
          "needle": "(",
          "regex": "(?i)(sprintf|snprintf|strcat|strcpy)\\s*\\([^;]*\\b(select|insert|update|delete)\\b"
        },
        {
          "name": "Process.Start or SqlCommand with a built string",
          "langs": [
            "cs"
          ],
          "needle": "(",
          "regex": "Process\\.Start\\s*\\(\\s*\"(cmd|sh|bash)|new\\s+SqlCommand\\s*\\(\\s*(\\$\"|\"[^\"]*\"\\s*\\+|string\\.Format)|FromSqlRaw\\s*\\(\\s*\\$\"|ExecuteSqlRaw\\s*\\(\\s*\\$\""
        },
        {
          "name": "BinaryFormatter or unsafe serializer",
          "langs": [
            "cs"
          ],
          "needle": "new ",
          "regex": "new\\s+(BinaryFormatter|NetDataContractSerializer|SoapFormatter|LosFormatter|ObjectStateFormatter)\\s*\\("
        },
        {
          "name": "eval of a variable",
          "langs": [
            "sh"
          ],
          "needle": "eval",
          "regex": "\\beval\\s+.*\\$"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "access-control",
      "name": "Access control",
      "applies": {
        "content": [
          "(?i)\\b(login_required|authenticate|authorize|authorization|permission|is_admin|isAdmin|require_role|requireAuth|ensureAuth|passport\\.|jwt\\.|bearer|api[_-]?key|current_user|request\\.user|session\\[)"
        ]
      },
      "invariant": "Every handler that reads or changes a resource checks that this caller may act on this resource, through the same mechanism as its siblings.",
      "look": [
        "The handler list below: for each handler that changes state, where is the authorization check, and does it check the resource (this user owns record 42), not only that a session exists?",
        "Two paths to the same state change (UI route and API route, single and bulk, import and create): do both check the same thing?",
        "Fields copied from the request body into a record: can the caller set owner_id, role, is_admin, price, tenant?",
        "Identifiers from the request (ids, slugs, paths): is the lookup scoped to the caller (WHERE owner = current user), or global?",
        "Middleware order: does the auth middleware run before every route, including ones registered later, under another prefix, or on another server instance?",
        "Health, metrics, debug, admin, internal and export routes: who may reach them?"
      ],
      "counts": "A caller reaches an action or a record outside their authority: another user's data, an admin action, a field only the server should set.",
      "hardening": "A check that exists but is written differently from its siblings, a missing rate limit, an internal route that only operators can reach by deployment facts you cannot read (needs_validation).",
      "patterns": [
        {
          "name": "route handler",
          "langs": [
            "py"
          ],
          "needle": "@",
          "regex": "@\\w+\\.(route|get|post|put|patch|delete|api_route|websocket)\\s*\\(|^\\s*(path|re_path|url)\\s*\\(\\s*[\"']"
        },
        {
          "name": "route handler",
          "langs": [
            "js"
          ],
          "needle": ".",
          "regex": "\\b(app|router|server|fastify|api)\\.(get|post|put|patch|delete|all|use)\\s*\\(\\s*[\"'`/]|export\\s+(async\\s+)?function\\s+(GET|POST|PUT|PATCH|DELETE)\\b|@(Get|Post|Put|Patch|Delete)\\s*\\("
        },
        {
          "name": "route handler",
          "langs": [
            "go"
          ],
          "needle": "(",
          "regex": "\\.(HandleFunc|Handle|GET|POST|PUT|PATCH|DELETE|Any|Group)\\s*\\(\\s*\"|http\\.HandleFunc\\s*\\("
        },
        {
          "name": "route handler",
          "langs": [
            "rs"
          ],
          "needle": "route",
          "regex": "\\.route\\s*\\(\\s*\"|#\\[(get|post|put|patch|delete|route)\\s*\\(|\\.service\\s*\\(|web::(get|post|put|patch|delete)\\s*\\(\\)"
        },
        {
          "name": "route handler",
          "langs": [
            "java"
          ],
          "needle": "Mapping",
          "regex": "@(Get|Post|Put|Patch|Delete|Request)Mapping\\b|@Path\\s*\\("
        },
        {
          "name": "route handler",
          "langs": [
            "rb"
          ],
          "needle": " ",
          "regex": "^\\s*(get|post|put|patch|delete|resources?|match)\\s+[\"':]"
        },
        {
          "name": "route handler",
          "langs": [
            "php"
          ],
          "needle": "Route",
          "regex": "Route::(get|post|put|patch|delete|any|match|resource)\\s*\\("
        },
        {
          "name": "route handler",
          "langs": [
            "cs"
          ],
          "needle": "[Http",
          "regex": "\\[Http(Get|Post|Put|Patch|Delete)\\b|\\.Map(Get|Post|Put|Patch|Delete)\\s*\\("
        },
        {
          "name": "mass assignment from the request",
          "langs": [
            "py"
          ],
          "needle": "request",
          "regex": "\\*\\*\\s*(request\\.(json|form|data|args|POST|GET)|data|payload|body)\\b|\\.update\\s*\\(\\s*request\\.(json|form|data|POST)"
        },
        {
          "name": "mass assignment from the request",
          "langs": [
            "js"
          ],
          "needle": "req.",
          "regex": "(\\.\\.\\.req\\.(body|query|params)|Object\\.assign\\s*\\([^,]+,\\s*req\\.(body|query)|\\.(create|update|insertMany|updateOne|findOneAndUpdate)\\s*\\(\\s*req\\.body)"
        },
        {
          "name": "role or admin from the request",
          "langs": [
            "any"
          ],
          "needle": "r",
          "regex": "(?i)(req(uest)?\\.(body|query|params|json|form|args|data)\\s*(\\[|\\.|\\.get\\()\\s*[\"']?(role|is_admin|isAdmin|admin|owner_id|user_id|tenant_id|org_id|price|amount|balance)\\b)"
        },
        {
          "name": "authorization turned off",
          "langs": [
            "any"
          ],
          "needle": "=",
          "regex": "(?i)\\b(permission_classes|authentication_classes)\\s*=\\s*(\\[\\s*\\]|\\(\\s*\\)|\\[\\s*AllowAny)|@csrf_exempt|\\bskip_authorization\\b|\\bauth\\s*[:=]\\s*(false|False|None|null)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "files-resources",
      "name": "Files, paths, archives and outbound requests",
      "applies": {
        "langs": [
          "py",
          "js",
          "go",
          "rs",
          "java",
          "rb",
          "php",
          "c",
          "cs",
          "swift",
          "sh"
        ]
      },
      "invariant": "A path or URL from outside stays inside the intended folder or host set; archives are checked member by member; temporary files are private.",
      "look": [
        "A path built from a request value, a file name or an argument: is it resolved and checked to stay under the base folder (resolve then is_relative_to / Rel without ..)? Is the client's file name used as the stored name?",
        "Archive extraction: members with .. or absolute paths, symlinks, size limits (zip bomb).",
        "An outbound request to a URL from outside (webhook, callback, fetch, import by URL): allowlisted scheme and host, no loopback or private addresses, redirects not followed into them (SSRF).",
        "Downloads and sendFile with a user path; static file servers with a root above the intended folder.",
        "Temporary files with fixed names in /tmp, or created then opened by path (TOCTOU); world-readable modes.",
        "Uploads: size limit, content type checked by content not by name, stored outside the web root, under a generated name."
      ],
      "counts": "A lower-trust party reads or writes a file outside the intended folder, or makes the server fetch an internal address, with a concrete result.",
      "hardening": "A check that exists in another form (containment by chroot or a sandbox you read), a missing limit without a reachable effect.",
      "patterns": [
        {
          "name": "path built from a request value",
          "langs": [
            "py"
          ],
          "needle": "request",
          "regex": "(os\\.path\\.join|open|Path|send_file|send_from_directory)\\s*\\([^)]*request\\.(args|form|json|files|values|data|path|view_args)|\\.filename\\b"
        },
        {
          "name": "archive extracted without a check",
          "langs": [
            "py"
          ],
          "needle": "extract",
          "regex": "\\.extractall\\s*\\((?![^)]*filter)|(zip|tar|archive|zf|tf|z|t|bundle)\\w*\\.extract\\s*\\("
        },
        {
          "name": "outbound request to a variable URL",
          "langs": [
            "py"
          ],
          "needle": "(",
          "regex": "\\b(requests\\.(get|post|put|delete|head|request)|urlopen|httpx\\.(get|post)|aiohttp\\.ClientSession\\(\\)\\.get)\\s*\\(\\s*[a-zA-Z_f][\\w.\\[\\]\"']*\\s*[,)]"
        },
        {
          "name": "verify disabled",
          "langs": [
            "py"
