    {
      "id": "crypto-secrets",
      "name": "Cryptography, randomness and secret handling",
      "applies": {
        "content": [
          "(?i)\\b(hashlib|bcrypt|argon2|scrypt|pbkdf2|hmac|crypto\\.|Cipher|AES|RSA|jwt|jsonwebtoken|jose|md5|sha1|random\\.|Math\\.random|rand\\.|SecureRandom|secrets\\.|token_hex|randomBytes)\\b"
        ]
      },
      "invariant": "Security values come from a cryptographic random source, passwords are hashed with a slow hash, secrets are compared in constant time, and failures never fall back to no protection.",
      "look": [
        "Tokens, session ids, reset codes, nonces, IVs made with random/Math.random/rand.Intn instead of secrets/crypto.randomBytes/crypto/rand/SecureRandom.",
        "Passwords hashed with md5, sha1 or sha256 (fast hashes) or stored plain; API keys compared with == instead of a constant-time compare.",
        "AES in ECB mode, a static or reused IV or nonce, encryption without authentication (no GCM/HMAC), a key derived from a password without a KDF.",
        "A secret read from code or a default value when the environment variable is missing (SECRET_KEY = os.environ.get('SECRET_KEY', 'dev')).",
        "What happens when a crypto operation fails: does the error path skip verification or return success?",
        "Secrets in logs, error messages, URLs (query strings), responses, or client bundles."
      ],
      "counts": "A token or key a lower-trust party can predict, forge or read; a password store a leaked database would reveal; a verification an attacker can skip.",
      "hardening": "A fast hash of a non-secret, a weak random for a non-security value (a display id, a shuffle), a default secret used only in tests you read.",
      "patterns": [
        {
          "name": "weak random for a token",
          "langs": [
            "py"
          ],
          "needle": "random",
          "regex": "\\brandom\\.(random|randint|choice|choices|getrandbits|randrange|shuffle)\\s*\\([^\\n]*(token|secret|key|nonce|salt|session|password|otp|code|csrf|reset)|(token|secret|nonce|salt|session|otp|reset)\\w*\\s*=\\s*[^\\n]*\\brandom\\.(random|randint|choice|choices|getrandbits|randrange)"
        },
        {
          "name": "fast hash of a password",
          "langs": [
            "py"
          ],
          "needle": "hashlib",
          "regex": "hashlib\\.(md5|sha1|sha224|sha256|sha512)\\s*\\([^\\n]*(password|passwd|pwd)"
        },
        {
          "name": "default secret value",
          "langs": [
            "py"
          ],
          "needle": "SECRET",
          "regex": "(?i)(secret_key|secret|jwt_secret|signing_key|api_key)\\w*\\s*=\\s*os\\.(environ\\.get|getenv)\\s*\\([^,)]+,\\s*[\"'][^\"']+[\"']\\s*\\)"
        },
        {
          "name": "ECB mode or a static IV",
