          "(?i)\\b(tenant_id|tenantId|org_id|orgId|organization_id|account_id|owner_id|user_id|userId|to_dict|model_to_dict|as_dict|jsonify|toJSON|res\\.json|c\\.JSON)\\b"
        ]
      },
      "invariant": "Every read, list, search, export and derived copy is scoped to the caller's tenant and ownership, and returns only the fields the caller may see.",
      "look": [
        "Queries that look a record up by id without the tenant or owner in the WHERE clause; list and count endpoints without a scope; raw or unscoped query clients.",
        "Serializers that return whole records (to_dict, model_to_dict, jsonify(user), select *): password hashes, tokens, internal flags, other users' fields.",
        "Export, backup, report and bulk download: do they apply per-item authorization after selection? Deleted, draft or private items included?",
        "Import and restore: can they overwrite records, set owner fields, create records in another tenant?",
        "Search, filter, sort and error messages as oracles: do they reveal existence or values of items the caller cannot read (different message, count or ordering)?",
        "Caches, indexes, thumbnails, feeds and logs: keyed without the tenant, or not invalidated when access changes."
